## CaaS Hosted Cluster ({{ _hc_name }})

| | |
|---|---|
| **API** | `https://{{ _hc_api }}` |
| **Console** | `https://{{ _caas_console.stdout | default('console-openshift-console.apps.' + _hc_name + '.' + ocp_base_domain, true) }}` |
| **User** | `kubeadmin` |
| **Password** | `{{ _caas_kubeadmin.stdout }}` |
| **Workers** | {{ _caas_nodes.stdout | default('N/A', true) }} |

### Copy kubeconfig to laptop

```bash
scp root@{{ _bm_ip }}:/tmp/caas-kubeconfig.yaml ~/.kube/caas-{{ lab_name }}.yaml
export KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/caas-{{ lab_name }}.yaml
oc get nodes
```

Or regenerate from the management cluster:

```bash
export KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/ocp-{{ lab_name }}.yaml
oc get secret -n {{ _hc_namespace }}-{{ _hc_name }} admin-kubeconfig \
  -o jsonpath='{.data.kubeconfig}' | base64 -d > ~/.kube/caas-{{ lab_name }}.yaml
```

### Login with oc CLI

```bash
oc login https://{{ _hc_api }} \
  --username=kubeadmin \
  --password='{{ _caas_kubeadmin.stdout }}' \
  --insecure-skip-tls-verify
```

